IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `euca-nouns`
IMPORT `euca-shared`

-- Section 202(a)(3): the work test. Layer 1: the law, objectively.
-- No extended compensation "under this Act" for a week in the individual's eligibility period in
-- which the individual fails to accept suitable work, to apply for referred suitable work, or to
-- actively engage in seeking work; and the ineligibility goes on until the individual has worked
-- four weeks for enough pay. The relation: the State (and, through it, the State agency) holds no
-- duty to pay for such a week (and may not be reimbursed for paying it, s 202(a)(6)); the individual
-- holds no claim for it. Subparagraph D lists the offers the individual may refuse without penalty.
-- out of text: what the State agency finds satisfactory (C), what State law treats as suitable (C),
-- what State law would deny (D)(iii), the wages of the position and the minimum wages (D)(iv):
-- all of these are plain inputs in the records declared in euca-nouns.

§ `Section 202(a)(3): the work test`

§§ `202(a)(3)(C): suitable work`

-- src:38 | For purposes of this paragraph, the term ‘suitable work’ means, with respect to any individual, any work which is within such individual’s capabilities; except that, if the individual furnishes evidence satisfactory to the State agency that such individual’s prospects for obtaining work in his customary occupation within a reasonably short period are good, the determination of whether any work is suitable work with respect to such individual shall be made in accordance with the applicable State law.
@ref s 202(a)(3)(C) (src:38)
GIVEN offer IS AN `Offer of work or referral`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the work is suitable work` offer MEANS
    IF offer's `the individual furnished evidence satisfactory to the State agency that prospects of work in the customary occupation are good`
    THEN offer's `the applicable State law treats the work as suitable`
    ELSE offer's `the work is within the individual's capabilities`

§§ `202(a)(3)(D): offers the individual may turn down without being denied`

-- src:39 | “(D) Extended compensation shall not be denied under clause (i) of subparagraph (A) to any individual for any week by reason of a failure to accept an offer of, or apply for, suitable work—
-- src:40 | “(i) if the gross average weekly remuneration payable to such individual for the position does not exceed the sum of—
-- src:41 | “(I) the individual’s average weekly benefit amount (as determined for purposes of subsection (b)(1)(C)) for his benefit year, plus
-- src:42 | “(II) the amount (if any) of supplemental unemployment compensation benefits (as defined in section 501(c)(17)(D) of the Internal Revenue Code of 1986) payable to such individual for such week;
@ref s 202(a)(3)(D)(i) (src:39-42)
GIVEN offer IS AN `Offer of work or referral`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the pay for the position does not exceed the benefit amount plus supplemental benefits` offer MEANS
    offer's `gross average weekly remuneration payable for the position` AT MOST
        (  offer's `average weekly benefit amount for the individual's benefit year`
         PLUS offer's `supplemental unemployment compensation benefits payable to the individual for the week`)

-- src:43 | “(ii) if the position was not offered to such individual in writing and was not listed with the State employment service;
@ref s 202(a)(3)(D)(ii) (src:43)
GIVEN offer IS AN `Offer of work or referral`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the position was neither offered in writing nor listed with the State employment service` offer MEANS
        (NOT offer's `the position was offered to the individual in writing`)
    AND (NOT offer's `the position was listed with the State employment service`)

-- src:44 | “(iii) if such failure would not result in a denial of compensation under the provisions of the applicable State law to the extent that such provisions are not inconsistent with the provisions of subparagraphs (C) and (E); or
@ref s 202(a)(3)(D)(iii) (src:44)
GIVEN offer IS AN `Offer of work or referral`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the failure would not result in a denial under the State law` offer MEANS
    NOT offer's `State law, so far as consistent with C and E, would deny compensation for the failure`

-- src:45 | “(iv) if the position pays wages less than the higher of—
-- src:46 | “(I) the minimum wage provided by section 6(a)(1) of the Fair Labor Standards Act of 1938 [29 U.S.C. 206(a)(1)], without regard to any exemption; or
-- src:47 | “(II) any applicable State or local minimum wage.
@ref s 202(a)(3)(D)(iv) (src:45-47)
GIVEN offer IS AN `Offer of work or referral`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the position pays less than the higher of the minimum wages` offer MEANS
    offer's `wages the position pays per hour` LESS THAN
        (`the greater of two amounts`
            (offer's `Fair Labor Standards Act section 6(a)(1) minimum wage per hour, without regard to any exemption`)
            (offer's `highest applicable State or local minimum wage per hour, or 0 if there is none`))

-- Any one of clauses (i) to (iv) is enough: the four are separated by ";" and the third by "or".
-- src:39 | “(D) Extended compensation shall not be denied under clause (i) of subparagraph (A) to any individual for any week by reason of a failure to accept an offer of, or apply for, suitable work—
@ref s 202(a)(3)(D) (src:39)
GIVEN offer IS AN `Offer of work or referral`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`an exception in subparagraph D applies` offer MEANS
        `the pay for the position does not exceed the benefit amount plus supplemental benefits` offer
    OR  `the position was neither offered in writing nor listed with the State employment service` offer
    OR  `the failure would not result in a denial under the State law` offer
    OR  `the position pays less than the higher of the minimum wages` offer

§§ `202(a)(3)(A)(i): failing to accept suitable work or to apply for referred work`

-- src:28 | “(3)
-- src:29 | (A) Notwithstanding the provisions of paragraph (2), payment of extended compensation under this Act [see Short Title of 1970 Amendment note set out under section 3311 of this title] shall not be made to any individual for any week of unemployment in his eligibility period—
-- src:30 | “(i) during which he fails to accept any offer of suitable work (as defined in subparagraph (c) [probably means subpar. (C)]) or fails to apply for any suitable work to which he was referred by the State agency; or
@ref s 202(a)(3)(A)(i) (src:28-30)
GIVEN offer IS AN `Offer of work or referral`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the individual fails to accept an offer of suitable work or to apply for suitable work to which referred` offer MEANS
        `the work is suitable work` offer
    AND CONSIDER offer's `how the work reached the individual`
        WHEN `offered to the individual` THEN NOT offer's `the individual accepted the offer`
        WHEN `referred to the individual by the State agency` THEN NOT offer's `the individual applied for the work to which the State agency referred them`

-- The failure bars extended compensation unless an exception in subparagraph D applies.
-- src:39 | “(D) Extended compensation shall not be denied under clause (i) of subparagraph (A) to any individual for any week by reason of a failure to accept an offer of, or apply for, suitable work—
@ref s 202(a)(3)(A)(i) and (D) (src:39)
GIVEN offer IS AN `Offer of work or referral`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`extended compensation is denied under clause (i) for the offer or referral` offer MEANS
        `the individual fails to accept an offer of suitable work or to apply for suitable work to which referred` offer
    AND (NOT `an exception in subparagraph D applies` offer)

-- src:29 | shall not be made to any individual for any week of unemployment in his eligibility period
@ref s 202(a)(3)(A)(i) (src:29)
GIVEN offers IS A LIST OF `Offer of work or referral`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`extended compensation is denied under clause (i) for any offer or referral` offers MEANS
    any (GIVEN offer YIELD `extended compensation is denied under clause (i) for the offer or referral` offer) offers

§§ `202(a)(3)(E): actively engaged in seeking work`

-- src:48 | “(E) For purposes of this paragraph, an individual shall be treated as actively engaged in seeking work during any week if—
-- src:49 | “(i) the individual has engaged in a systematic and sustained effort to obtain work during such week, and
-- src:50 | “(ii) the individual provides tangible evidence to the State agency that he has engaged in such an effort during such week.
@ref s 202(a)(3)(E) (src:48-50)
GIVEN search IS A `Search for work`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the individual is treated as actively engaged in seeking work` search MEANS
        search's `engaged in a systematic and sustained effort to obtain work during the week`
    AND search's `provided tangible evidence to the State agency of that effort`

§§ `202(a)(3)(A)(ii): failing to actively engage in seeking work`

-- The exemptions in clauses (I) and (II) are read one by one: each needs its own two conditions.
-- See the fork register.
-- src:32 | before any court of the United States or any State pursuant to a lawfully issued summons to appear for jury duty
-- src:34 | if such exemptions in clauses (I) and (II) apply to recipients of regular benefits, and the State chooses to apply such exemptions for recipients of extended benefits.
@ref s 202(a)(3)(A)(ii)(I) (src:32 src:34)
GIVEN search IS A `Search for work`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the jury duty exemption applies` search MEANS
        search's `before a court of the United States or of a State pursuant to a lawfully issued summons to appear for jury duty`
    AND search's `the jury duty exemption applies to recipients of regular benefits`
    AND search's `the State chooses to apply the jury duty exemption to recipients of extended benefits`

-- src:33 | “(II) hospitalized for treatment of an emergency or a life-threatening condition (as such term may be defined by such Secretary),
-- src:34 | if such exemptions in clauses (I) and (II) apply to recipients of regular benefits, and the State chooses to apply such exemptions for recipients of extended benefits.
@ref s 202(a)(3)(A)(ii)(II) (src:33-34)
GIVEN search IS A `Search for work`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the hospitalization exemption applies` search MEANS
        search's `hospitalized for treatment of an emergency or a life-threatening condition`
    AND search's `the hospitalization exemption applies to recipients of regular benefits`
    AND search's `the State chooses to apply the hospitalization exemption to recipients of extended benefits`

-- src:31 | during which he fails to actively engage in seeking work, unless such individual is not actively engaged in seeking work because such individual is, as determined in accordance with State law—
@ref s 202(a)(3)(A)(ii) (src:31)
GIVEN search IS A `Search for work`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`extended compensation is denied under clause (ii) for failing to seek work` search MEANS
        (NOT `the individual is treated as actively engaged in seeking work` search)
    AND (NOT (   `the jury duty exemption applies` search
              OR `the hospitalization exemption applies` search))

§§ `202(a)(3)(B): how long the ineligibility lasts`

-- The period begins with the week after the week of the failure and does not end until the
-- individual has been employed for at least 4 weeks that began after the failure, with total
-- remuneration of not less than 4 times the average weekly benefit amount.
-- src:35 | “(B) If any individual is ineligible for extended compensation for any week by reason of a failure described in clause (i) or (ii) of subparagraph (A), the individual shall be ineligible to receive extended compensation for any week which begins during a period which—
-- src:36 | “(i) begins with the week following the week in which such failure occurs, and
-- src:37 | “(ii) does not end until such individual has been employed during at least 4 weeks which begin after such failure and the total of the remuneration earned by the individual for being so employed is not less than the product of 4 multiplied by the individual’s average weekly benefit amount (as determined for purposes of subsection (b)(1)(c) [probably means subsec. (b)(1)(C)]) for his benefit year.
@ref s 202(a)(3)(B) (src:35-37)
GIVEN failure IS AN `Earlier failure`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the period of ineligibility after an earlier failure has ended` failure MEANS
        failure's `weeks of employment that began after the failure and before the week claimed` AT LEAST 4
    AND failure's `remuneration earned for being so employed` AT LEAST
        (4 TIMES failure's `average weekly benefit amount for the individual's benefit year`)

-- src:36 | begins with the week following the week in which such failure occurs
@ref s 202(a)(3)(B)(i) (src:36)
GIVEN week IS A DATE
      failure IS AN `Earlier failure`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the week begins during the period of ineligibility after an earlier failure` week failure MEANS
    CONSIDER failure's `week in which the failure occurred, if there was one`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST failed THEN
            week AT LEAST (`the week that falls this many weeks after` failed 1)
        AND (NOT `the period of ineligibility after an earlier failure has ended` failure)

-- src:37 | such individual has been employed during at least 4 weeks which begin after such failure
@ref s 202(a)(3)(B)(ii) (src:37)
GIVEN failure IS AN `Earlier failure`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`weeks of employment still needed to end the period of ineligibility` failure MEANS
    `the greater of two amounts` 0 (4 MINUS failure's `weeks of employment that began after the failure and before the week claimed`)

-- src:37 | the total of the remuneration earned by the individual for being so employed is not less than the product of 4 multiplied by the individual’s average weekly benefit amount
@ref s 202(a)(3)(B)(ii) (src:37)
GIVEN failure IS AN `Earlier failure`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`remuneration still needed to end the period of ineligibility` failure MEANS
    `the greater of two amounts` 0
        ((4 TIMES failure's `average weekly benefit amount for the individual's benefit year`) MINUS failure's `remuneration earned for being so employed`)

§§ `202(a)(3)(A) to (E) together: whether the work test bars extended compensation for the week`

-- src:29 | Notwithstanding the provisions of paragraph (2), payment of extended compensation under this Act [see Short Title of 1970 Amendment note set out under section 3311 of this title] shall not be made to any individual for any week of unemployment in his eligibility period
@ref s 202(a)(3)(A), (B) (src:29)
GIVEN week IS A DATE
      offers IS A LIST OF `Offer of work or referral`
      search IS A `Search for work`
      failure IS AN `Earlier failure`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the work test bars extended compensation for the week` week offers search failure MEANS
        `extended compensation is denied under clause (i) for any offer or referral` offers
    OR  `extended compensation is denied under clause (ii) for failing to seek work` search
    OR  `the week begins during the period of ineligibility after an earlier failure` week failure

§§ `202(a)(3)(F): the work the State law must refer applicants to`

-- src:51 | “(F) For purposes of section 3304(a)(11) of the Internal Revenue Code of 1986, a State law shall provide for referring applicants for benefits under this Act [see Short Title of 1970 Amendment note set out under section 3311 of this title] to any suitable work to which clauses (i), (ii), (iii), and (iv) of subparagraph (D) would not apply.
@ref s 202(a)(3)(F) (src:51)
GIVEN offer IS AN `Offer of work or referral`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the State law must provide for referring applicants to the work` offer MEANS
        `the work is suitable work` offer
    AND (NOT `an exception in subparagraph D applies` offer)
